Priority: 3
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-multi-select, add-image-paste, add-pdf-page-import-and-recolor

Goal:
Add a double-press `Space` shortcut that fits the camera to the full canvas content, so all strokes, shapes, text, images, and imported PDF pages become visible in the viewport at once.

Context:
The user wants a quick “fit zoom” action tied to a double press of `Space`. The app already has pan/zoom camera logic, so this task should compute the aggregate content bounds and reposition plus rescale the camera to fit everything inside the visible canvas viewport with reasonable padding.

Expected changes:

- inspect the current camera model and `Space` handling in the canvas workspace
- add double-press detection for `Space` without breaking the existing hold-to-pan behavior
- compute aggregate canvas bounds across every visible element type
- update camera position and zoom so the full content set fits in the viewport

Acceptance criteria:

- Double pressing `Space` fits all current canvas content into view.
- The fit logic includes strokes, shapes, text items, pasted images, and imported PDF page placements.
- Existing single-press or hold `Space` camera behavior still works.
- Empty-canvas behavior is safe and does not produce invalid camera math.
- `npm run build` and `cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml` pass.

Notes:

- Add padding so content is not flush against the viewport edges.
- Guard against zero-size bounds and invalid zoom values.
